          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><h3>Annotation</h3><table class=\"hl7__eu__lab__report\"><tr><th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th></tr><tr><td>Renal function is mildly decreased (GFR 65 mL/min/1.73 m²), consistent with age-related decline. Urine albumin/creatinine ratio is at the upper limit of normal (28 mg/g), suggesting no significant albuminuria. Overall, results indicate stable, age-appropriate kidney function without evidence of significant renal impairment or proteinuria. Recommend continued monitoring.</td></tr></table></div>"
